course: dictionary
lesson: 9180
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them, and the sentence tells you which one fits. The word soapy has three: full of soap, like soap in taste, smell or feel, and, in informal talk, too dramatic. «Wash your hands with soapy water for about 20 seconds.» Here soapy means full of soap.
explain: «Lick a lemon and it is sour; taste a tiny pinch of baking soda and it is bitter and soapy.» Nobody is washing anything here, so soapy must describe a taste, like soap. Look at the clues: the sentence is about tasting, not about bubbles.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «Skin stuck with super glue is soaked in warm soapy water and gently rolled apart.» Soapy water is water with soap in it, and that fits.
fact: Soapy has three meanings: full of soap, like soap in taste, smell or feel, and informal: like a soap opera, too dramatic and emotional.
fact: «Soapy water» means water with soap in it.
fact: Soapy floors and bathtubs are slippery, so walk carefully and be safe.
fact: Soapy water makes bubbles, and it can break up grease and germs.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: «Wash your hands with soapy water for about 20 seconds.» What does soapy mean here? | Like a soap opera | Sour and bitter | *Full of soap | Very wet from rain
exercise: «Lick a lemon and it is sour; taste a tiny pinch of baking soda and it is bitter and soapy.» What does soapy mean in this sentence? | Full of soap bubbles | Too dramatic and emotional | *Like soap in taste | Clean and shiny
exercise: Why are «soapy floors» dangerous? | They smell of lemons | *They are slippery | They are too dramatic | They are sticky like glue
test: Ella says, «That film was so soapy, with everyone shouting and crying all the time.» What does soapy mean? | Full of soap | Like soap in taste | *Like a soap opera, too dramatic and emotional | Covered in bubbles
test: «In soapy water the air escaping from a punctured tube makes bubbles that show where the hole is.» What do the bubbles show? | The colour of the tube | How much soap is in the water | *The place where the hole is | The time of day
exam: Ravi says soapy only means covered in soap. Is he right? | *No, it can also mean like soap in taste, or too dramatic | No, it means happy | Yes, but only in the bath | Yes, it has only one meaning
